### 4. Self-Improving Error Attribution (Loop-Level)

#### [MODIFY] [storage.py](file:///c:/Users/yasha/Desktop/Flight%20Finder/backend/predictor/storage.py) & [price_predictor.py](file:///c:/Users/yasha/Desktop/Flight%20Finder/backend/price_predictor.py)
- **Root Cause Error Classification**:
  - In the 30-day auditing loop, when MAPE is $>25\%$, evaluate the date against active indicators:
    - Check if news reports showed weather events (`natural_disaster_at_destination` $\rightarrow$ "Monsoon/Storm").
    - Check if prices dropped below 15th percentile overnight $\rightarrow$ "Unpredicted Flash Sale".
    - Check if travel dates coincided with CBSE boards $\rightarrow$ "Board Exam Shift".
  - Log the classified cause to a new database table `error_attribution`.
  - Automatically adjust the weights of these features (e.g., dampening news advisory weight if it produced false positives) by updating a dynamic multiplier table read by the XGBoost pipeline.

